---
/*
  CONTACT, rebuilt 2026-08-10 as the calmest page on the site.

  WHAT WAS WRONG. Four facts, five typographic registers, and the hierarchy
  upside down. It ran display for the word "Contatti", body for the intro,
  label for three headings, mono for the two addresses, and two more mark
  treatments on top. The two things a reader comes here to get — the handle and
  the email — were the SMALLEST type on the page at 12px, sitting under 11px
  labels that named what the strings already said, while the page's largest
  voice was spent on a word repeated from the menu the reader just used.

  THREE CHANGES, and each removes something rather than adding:

  1. MONO IS GONE. The token says what it is for: DATA ONLY, prices,
     measurements, counts (tokens.css). An email address is not a measurement.
     It was mono because it looks technical, which is the opposite of a reason.
     Both addresses are body register now — the register for things a person
     reads — and they are the largest readable type on the page as a result.

  2. THE DEFINITION LIST IS GONE, and with it the two labels above it. A line
     reading "@aleksandercecco" does not need a heading that says Instagram,
     and one reading "aleksandercecco@gmail.com" does not need a heading that
     says Email; the strings are self-identifying, and the glyph beside the
     handle names it for a screen reader. The footer settled this argument
     already: it is an inscription, not headed cells (section 26), and this
     page is the same four facts.

  3. SEPARATION IS WHITESPACE, not a rule. The menu separates its two groups
     by whitespace alone (section 67) and this page borrows that: one wide gap
     between the two ways to reach the brand and the terms of buying from it.
     No hairline, no second device. The spine is already drawing the only line
     this surface gets.

  What is left is display once, label once, body for everything else. Marks
  stay exactly as they were: they are the honesty contract, not decoration, and
  three facts here have three different standings.

  The address is the brand's own from 2026-08-03. The placeholder guard stays:
  anything at example.com is NEVER rendered as a working mailto link, because a
  live link to a fake address is worse than no link at all.
*/
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import InstagramMark from "../../components/InstagramMark.astro";
import PairedSurface from "../../components/PairedSurface.astro";
import {getSiteSettings, isPlaceholderEmail, isPlaceholderText} from "../../lib/content";
import type {MediaItem} from "../../lib/media";
import {LOCALES, localePath, pick, toLocale} from "../../lib/locales";
import {isMarked, voiceState} from "../../lib/voice";
import {t} from "../../i18n/ui";
import {SHOW_UNAPPROVED_MARKS} from "../../lib/marks";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return LOCALES.map((lang) => ({params: {lang}}));
}

const locale = toLocale(Astro.params.lang);
const settings = await getSiteSettings();

const instagramUrl = settings.instagramUrl?.trim() || null;
const instagramHandle = instagramUrl
  ? `@${instagramUrl.replace(/\/+$/, "").split("/").pop()}`
  : null;

const email = settings.contactEmail?.trim() || null;
const emailIsPlaceholder = isPlaceholderEmail(email);

const shipping = pick(settings.shippingReturns, locale);
const shippingIsPlaceholder = isPlaceholderText(shipping);

/*
  TWO LINES NOW, NOT THREE (2026-08-12, section 104). The free-shipping line is
  HIS fact in HIS words and is unmarked. The returns line is his fact in our
  wording and is marked as ours.

  The customs line is GONE — it said who normally pays duties outside the EU,
  which is a condition of sale, which is exactly the kind of claim nobody has
  checked since the shop changed twice this week. It was also flagged
  unconfirmed by us for a fortnight. Silence is not exposure; a wrong term is.
*/
const free = pick(settings.shippingFree, locale);

/*
  The shipping and returns text is OURS, not his, so it is a draft in every
  language rather than a translation, and it says so. The two facts in it are
  the owner's (worldwide, customer pays return shipping); the wording is not.
*/
const voice = voiceState(settings, locale, Boolean(settings.footerCopyIsDraft));
const shippingIsMarked =
  SHOW_UNAPPROVED_MARKS && isMarked(voice) && Boolean(shipping) && !shippingIsPlaceholder;
const notice = voice === "translation" ? "translationNotice" : "draftNotice";

/*
  THE ONE PHOTOGRAPH (2026-08-13, section 108).

  This was the last page on the site that was a COLUMN OF WORDS ALONE ON FLAT
  GROUND, which the four references were re-measured for and which appears in
  none of them (PairedSurface's own note). Measured at 1440: four facts and two
  short lines in a 1824px page, with the footer repeating the handle and the
  email inside the same screen — the page said everything it had, twice, in
  about a tenth of the room it took.

  So it is composed the way /about and /process are: one column beside one
  frame, photograph on the RIGHT so the two addresses stay exactly where they
  were, hard left, which is where a reader who came here for them will look.

  WHICH FRAME IS A CHOICE, AND THE CHOICE IS OURS UNTIL HE MAKES IT. He can set
  `contactMedia` in the studio and that wins. With nothing set the page takes
  the LAST frame of the about sequence — last because it is the head of no other
  composition on the site, and because with this dataset every frame is used
  somewhere, so "unused" was never available. That fallback is flagged
  `contactFrame` in inventedCopy exactly as our Instagram selection is, and
  `npm run launch-check` names it until he chooses.

  It falls all the way through to nothing: with no photographs at all the page
  renders as the plain column it used to be rather than failing.

  A FALLBACK MUST NOT PICK UP A CLIP (2026-08-17, section 125). It took the
  LAST frame of the about sequence, and on 2026-08-16 a video was appended to
  that sequence — so this page silently started playing the jacket loop, which
  nobody asked for and which /about was already showing. A frame chosen by
  position has to be filtered by what it IS, not trusted to stay a photograph.
*/
const stills = (frames: MediaItem[]) => frames.filter((m) => !m.videoUrl);
const aboutFrames = stills(settings.aboutMedia ?? []);
const processFrames = stills(settings.processMedia ?? []);
const contactFrame =
  settings.contactMedia ??
  aboutFrames.at(-1) ??
  processFrames.at(-1) ??
  settings.openingMedia ??
  null;
---

<Base locale={locale} title={t(locale, "contact")}>
  {/*
    THE COLUMN'S OWN HEIGHT, NOT THE VIEWPORT'S. `min-h-svh` and `pb-u21` were
    written when this page was a full screen of its own; inside a paired surface
    the floor is the composition's (56svh) and the padding is the surface's, and
    keeping both would put a screen of padding inside a screen.
  */}
  {/* `paired-inner` is already a u5 column at a 34rem measure, so the page adds
      no wrapper of its own. */}
  <PairedSurface media={contactFrame} locale={locale} side="right">
    <h1 class="type-display text-display">{t(locale, "contact")}</h1>
    <p class="type-body text-body max-w-prose">{t(locale, "contactIntro")}</p>

    {/*
      THE TWO WAYS IN. Body register, tight together, and nothing above them:
      these are the page's subject, so they are the largest readable thing on
      it. The glyph carries the word Instagram for a screen reader, which is
      what the deleted <dt> was for; sighted readers had the handle's own @ and
      never needed it.
    */}
    <div class="type-body text-body flex flex-col gap-u2 pt-u3">
      {
        instagramUrl ? (
          <a
            href={instagramUrl}
            rel="me noopener"
            target="_blank"
            class="flex items-center gap-u2 self-start hairline-under"
          >
            <InstagramMark title={t(locale, "instagram")} />
            {instagramHandle}
          </a>
        ) : (
          <span class="placeholder-mark self-start">{"{INSTAGRAM_URL}"}</span>
        )
      }

      {
        emailIsPlaceholder ? (
          <span class="placeholder-mark self-start">{"{CONTACT_EMAIL}"}</span>
        ) : (
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="self-start hairline-under">
            {email}
          </a>
        )
      }
    </div>

    {/*
      WHERE, AND WHAT NOT TO WRITE ABOUT (2026-08-17, section 125).

      The page had two addresses and two shipping lines and answered none of
      the questions a person actually arrives with. Two of them are answerable
      from facts already on the site, so they are answered here:

      - WHERE. A leather label's address is a trust signal and this one is
        good: the studio is in Naples and the hides are tanned an hour up the
        road. /about says it in his register; a reader who came to write to
        somebody should not have to go and find it.
      - WHETHER TO WRITE AT ALL. Every Creature already carries its own order
        form, and this page was quietly routing buyers into an inbox instead.
        Saying so here is the only sentence on the site that sends a reader
        AWAY from contact, and it is the most useful one on the page.

      Both are ours, carrying his facts, and flagged `contactCopy`.

      THE MADE-TO-MEASURE LINE THAT STOOD UNDER THEM IS GONE (2026-08-16,
      section 130). The owner decided there is no made to measure, so our
      sentence offering it "on request" stopped being an unapproved draft and
      became a false offer — here and on every piece page. Both went in the same
      change, which is what the handoff means by "when a decision changes, the
      same commit must change every place that argues the old one".
    */}
    <div class="type-body text-body flex flex-col gap-u2 pt-u8">
      <p class="max-w-prose">{t(locale, "contactWhere")}</p>
      <p class="max-w-prose">{t(locale, "contactBuy")}</p>
      <a href={localePath(locale, "creature")} class="self-start hairline-under">
        {t(locale, "allCreatures")}
      </a>
    </div>

    {/*
      The one wide gap: the ways in above it, the terms of buying below. u8
      rather than u13 since section 108 — the gap exists to separate two things,
      and inside a half-width column thirteen units separated them by most of a
      screen.
    */}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-u2 pt-u8">
      <h2 class="type-label text-label">{t(locale, "shippingReturns")}</h2>

      {/*
        HIS OWN FACT, in his own words, so it carries no mark at all and it goes
        first: free shipping over 500 euro is the most useful thing this page
        says to somebody deciding whether to ask (2026-08-03).
      */}
      {free && <p class="type-body text-body max-w-prose whitespace-pre-line">{free}</p>}

      {/*
        HOW LONG IT TAKES, which is a shipping fact and was only ever said on a
        piece's own page. Somebody deciding whether to write is asking it.
      */}

      {shippingIsMarked && <p class="placeholder-mark self-start">{t(locale, notice)}</p>}
      {
        shipping && !shippingIsPlaceholder ? (
          <p
            class:list={[
              "type-body text-body max-w-prose whitespace-pre-line",
              shippingIsMarked && "draft-text",
            ]}
          >
            {shipping}
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p class="placeholder-mark self-start">{shipping ?? "{SHIPPING_RETURNS}"}</p>
        )
      }

      {/*
        E IL TESTO INTERO (2026-08-17, sezione 137). La riga sopra dice i tre
        fatti che servono per decidere; questo link porta a quello che li
        governa. Sta qui perche' questa e' la sezione che parla di spedizione e
        resi, e chi ha una domanda piu' precisa e' gia' fermo su queste righe.
      */}
      <a href={localePath(locale, "terms")} class="type-label text-label self-start hairline-under">
        {t(locale, "returnsLink")}
      </a>

    </div>
  </PairedSurface>
</Base>
